# Security Rules (CRITICAL)

Read docs/SECURITY.md before writing any code in these files.

## Command Execution
- NEVER interpolate user input into shell commands: `` exec(`ls ${userPath}`) `` ← FORBIDDEN
- ALWAYS validate inputs before passing to SSH:
  - **Paths**: No traversal (`..`), must be absolute, use allowlist of base dirs
  - **Container IDs**: Hex characters only (`/^[a-f0-9]+$/`)
  - **PIDs**: Integer only (`/^\d+$/`)
  - **Service names**: Alphanumeric + hyphen + underscore only
- Use parameterized commands or builder functions:
  ```typescript
  // GOOD: Validated and constructed safely
  function buildLsCommand(validatedPath: string): string {
    return `ls -la ${shellEscape(validatedPath)}`;
  }

  // BAD: Direct interpolation
  function buildLsCommand(path: string): string {
    return `ls -la ${path}`; // ← NEVER DO THIS
  }
  ```

## File Operations
- ALL file read/write/delete/rename → SFTP API
- NEVER use `exec('cat ...')` or `exec('rm ...')` for file operations
- SFTP is the ONLY safe way to handle file content

## SSH Channel Safety
- `exec()` channels for one-shot data collection (parallel OK)
- `shell()` channel for interactive terminal only (one per session)
- Never reuse channels across requests
- Always set timeouts on exec channels
- Close channels when done — leaked channels = leaked resources

## Command Orchestrator Safety
- ExecutionPlan commands must come from registered command builders
- Retry logic must have max retry limits (default: 2)
- Fallback chains must terminate — no circular fallbacks
- LLM-suggested commands (future ReAct agent) must go through allowlist validation

## API Route Security
- Validate ALL request parameters with Zod schemas
- Use Fastify schema validation (built-in)
- Rate limit SSH-heavy endpoints
- Never expose raw SSH errors to the client — sanitize error messages

## Validation Functions
These MUST exist and be used everywhere:
```typescript
validatePath(path: string): boolean      // No traversal, absolute path
validateContainerId(id: string): boolean // Hex only
validatePid(pid: string): boolean        // Integer only
validateServiceName(name: string): boolean // Alphanumeric + hyphen + underscore
shellEscape(input: string): string       // Escape special chars for shell
```
